.TH TIMEKEEPER 1 "June 2026" "timekeeper 1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
timekeeper \- encode and decode Arvelie dates and Neralie time
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B timekeeper
[\fB--epoch\fR \fIYYYY-MM-DD\fR]
\fBencode-date\fR
\fIYYYY-M-D\fR
.PP
.B timekeeper
[\fB--epoch\fR \fIYYYY-MM-DD\fR]
\fBdecode-date\fR
\fIYYYY[A-Z|+]DD\fR
.PP
.B timekeeper
\fBencode-time\fR
\fIHH:MM:SS\fR
.PP
.B timekeeper
\fBdecode-time\fR
\fIBBB:PPP\fR
.PP
.B timekeeper
\fB--no-epoch\fR
\fBencode-date\fR
\fIYYYY-M-D\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B timekeeper
is a small command-line utility for converting between Gregorian dates,
Arvelie dates, standard clock time, and Neralie time.
.PP
Arvelie dates divide the year into 26 months of 14 days each. The months are
represented by the letters A through Z. The final extra day of a common year is
represented as
.BR +00 .
The final extra day of a leap year is represented as
.BR +01 .
.PP
Neralie time divides the day into 1000 beats. Each beat is divided into 1000
pulses. A Neralie time is written as
.BR BBB:PPP .
.PP
.B timekeeper
also supports an optional custom epoch. When an epoch is configured, Arvelie
year
.B 0000
starts on the configured epoch date.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B encode-date \fIYYYY-M-D\fR
Convert a Gregorian date to an Arvelie date.
.TP
.B decode-date \fIYYYY[A-Z|+]DD\fR
Convert an Arvelie date to a Gregorian date.
.TP
.B encode-time \fIHH:MM:SS\fR
Convert standard 24-hour time to Neralie time.
.TP
.B decode-time \fIBBB:PPP\fR
Convert Neralie time to standard 24-hour time.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI --epoch " YYYY-MM-DD"
Use a custom year-zero date for this command.
.TP
.BI --epoch= YYYY-MM-DD
Same as
.BR --epoch " " YYYY-MM-DD .
.TP
.B --no-epoch
Disable any configured epoch for this command. This is useful when an epoch is
set in the environment or config file, but the user wants normal Gregorian-year
Arvelie conversion for one command.
.SH DATE FORMAT
A normal Arvelie date has the form:
.PP
.RS
\fIYYYYMDD\fR
.RE
.PP
where
.I YYYY
is the Arvelie year,
.I M
is one of
.B A
through
.BR Z ,
and
.I DD
is the day within that 14-day month.
.PP
Examples:
.PP
.RS
2024A01
.br
2024B04
.br
2024Z14
.RE
.PP
The end-of-year overflow day is written with
.BR + :
.PP
.RS
2023+00
.br
2024+01
.RE
.SH TIME FORMAT
A Neralie time has the form:
.PP
.RS
\fIBBB:PPP\fR
.RE
.PP
where
.I BBB
is the beat, from 000 to 999, and
.I PPP
is the pulse, from 000 to 999.
.SH EPOCHS
The epoch controls the date that begins Arvelie year
.BR 0000 .
For example:
.PP
.RS
timekeeper --epoch 1990-05-12 encode-date 1990-05-12
.br
0000A01
.RE
.PP
The same epoch must be used when decoding an epoch-based Arvelie date:
.PP
.RS
timekeeper --epoch 1990-05-12 decode-date 0000A01
.br
1990-05-12
.RE
.PP
If a different epoch is used during decoding, the resulting Gregorian date will
be different.
.SH EPOCH SOURCE PRIORITY
Epoch configuration is loaded in this order:
.IP 1. 4
Command-line option:
.B --epoch
.I YYYY-MM-DD
or
.BI --epoch= YYYY-MM-DD
.IP 2. 4
Environment variable:
.B ARVELIE_EPOCH
.IP 3. 4
Config file:
.B $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/timekeeper/config
.IP 4. 4
Config file:
.B ~/.config/timekeeper/config
.PP
The command-line option has the highest priority.
.SH CONFIGURATION
The config file uses a simple key-value format:
.PP
.RS
epoch=1990-05-12
.RE
.PP
See
.BR timekeeper-config (5)
for more detail.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Encode a Gregorian date:
.B timekeeper encode-date 2024-1-18
.PP
.RS
2024B04
.RE
.TP
Decode an Arvelie date:
.B timekeeper decode-date 2024B04
.PP
.RS
2024-01-18
.RE
.TP
Encode midnight:
.B timekeeper encode-time 00:00:00
.PP
.RS
000:000
.RE
.TP
Encode 6 AM:
.B timekeeper encode-time 06:00:00
.PP
.RS
250:000
.RE
.TP
Decode Neralie noon:
.B timekeeper decode-time 500:000
.PP
.RS
12:00:00
.RE
.TP
Use a one-off epoch:
.B timekeeper --epoch 1990-05-12 encode-date 1990-05-12
.PP
.RS
0000A01
.RE
.TP
Disable configured epoch for one command:
.B timekeeper --no-epoch encode-date 1990-05-12
.PP
.RS
1990J06
.RE
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Invalid arguments, invalid input, or failed conversion.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/timekeeper/config
User config file when
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
is set.
.TP
.B ~/.config/timekeeper/config
Fallback user config file.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B ARVELIE_EPOCH
Sets the default custom epoch date. The expected format is
.IR YYYY-MM-DD .
.SH INSTALLATION
After building
.BR timekeeper ,
install the binary system-wide with:
.PP
.RS
sudo install -Dm755 timekeeper /usr/local/bin/timekeeper
.RE
.PP
Install this man page system-wide with:
.PP
.RS
sudo install -Dm644 timekeeper.1 /usr/local/share/man/man1/timekeeper.1
.br
sudo mandb
.RE
.PP
For a user-local install:
.PP
.RS
mkdir -p ~/.local/bin ~/.local/share/man/man1
.br
install -Dm755 timekeeper ~/.local/bin/timekeeper
.br
install -Dm644 timekeeper.1 ~/.local/share/man/man1/timekeeper.1
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR timekeeper-config (5),
.BR date (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Written for the timekeeper project.
